# Shared raptor base config. KEEP THIS FILE EMPTY.
#
# It exists only because pkg-kconfig errors out when
# THINGINO_RAPTOR_CONFIG_KCONFIG_FILE does not exist. It is not a place for
# settings.
#
# Why not: savedefconfig measures minimality against the "default" statements
# in the Kconfig, not against this file. A value set here is written straight
# back out by `make raptor-saveconfig` into <camera>/raptor.config, so that
# camera pins its own copy and later edits here never reach it. The sharing
# dies silently, one camera at a time.
#
# Shared and per-SoC defaults belong in package/thingino-raptor-config/Kconfig
# as conditional defaults, which savedefconfig understands and omits when a
# camera matches:
#
#   config RAPTOR_STREAM0_BITRATE
#   	string "bitrate (default 3000000)"
#   	default "2000000" if (RAPTOR_ENV_SOC_FAMILY = "t31")
#   	default ""
#
# See docs/dev/raptor-config.md
